RED
APPROACH
At first I was confused because the image was just a plain red square. I could not see anything useful in it.
I first thought maybe the flag was hidden in the image by changing some pixels or colors. I also looked at the hints again. The Red? Ged? Bed? Aed? hint made me think about the different color channels.
Then I noticed the last hint says to check whatever Facebook is called now. Facebook is called Meta so I thought maybe this was talking about metadata.
I tried checking the metadata online but one site said no metadata was found. So that did not work.
Then I tried an online steganography scanner. This gave me some hidden text results.
One of the results was a poem and another one was a long string that looked like Base64.

SOLUTION
I uploaded red.png to an online zsteg/LSB scanner.It showed a hidden text in metadata:
Crimson heart, vibrant and bold,
Hearts flutter at your sight.
Evenings glow softly red,
Cherries burst with sweet life.
Kisses linger with your warmth.
Love deep as merlot.
Scarlet leaves falling softly,
Bold in every stroke.

I took the first letter of each line:CHECKLSB
So I understood that I had to check the LSB of the image.
The scanner also found this hidden text:YWNhZGVteXtyM2RfMXNfdGgzX3VsdDFtNHQzX2N1cjNfZjByXzU0ZG4zNTVffQ==
It looked like Base64 because of the format and the = at the end.
I first thought the repeated string meant I had to decode the whole thing together, but then I realised the same Base64 text was just repeated multiple times. So I only used one copy.
I opened CyberChef and used the From Base64 operation.
The result was:academy{r3d_1s_th3_ult1m4t3_cur3_f0r_54dn355_}
So the flag was found by checking the image data for LSB hidden text and then decoding the Base64.
